  "note": "The filename slug says unknown: this is the UNHEADED continuation of the Lunenburg High School Faculty/Staff Roster begun on page 109 - identical four-sub-column x-positions (34 / 62-74 / 92-93 / 126-135) - so school is high. The heading governing L2-L4 right ('Social Studies') is printed on the previous page (p109 L39) and is carried over because the column continues unbroken. RULE 9 - the one-row shift. On five lines the title is rendered one line ABOVE its name and the name-only line follows: L1 'Teacher' (x=132) belongs to Casey McDonnell on L2; L6 'Teacher' (x=71) to Jennifer Biery on L7; L11 'Teacher' x=71 and x=132 to Taylor Smith and Scott Barry-Grove* on L12; L26 'Guidance' (x=132) to Jeff Dionne on L27; L30 'Para' (x=74) to Lisa Szocik-Maillett on L31. In every case the name on the line ABOVE the orphan title already carries its own title on its own line, which is what fixes the direction of the pairing. Those roles are therefore attributed to the name's line, not the title's line; L11 and L30 (title only) are ignored as continuations, while L1 and L6 also carry a section heading and are counted as heading lines. L17, L19, L22, L25 and L32 each carry a heading in one column and an entry in the other, so they are counted as entry lines. grade_or_dept is left empty for L39-L40 (Renee LaFountaine - Head Custodian, Richard Krafve - Custodian): the nearest heading above them in the right column is 'Cafeteria' (L35), which their own printed roles contradict, and the page prints no custodians heading. Pamela Vallee is printed twice, at L14 under Unified Arts and L23 under Media Specialist; both are recorded as printed. The asterisk on some names is printed on the page and has no legend on it."
